# sample_text in a browser: the page's tree enabled through its hidden
# button, as for the controls; then the Notes field as on the desktop,
# typed into, read by character, word and line, a selection made and
# deleted, the reader asked what has the focus as the walk reaches it.
key b
key Return
# The page builds its elements and the reader reads them anew: on the
# runner's SwiftShader the first control's focus was lost under 3 s.
wait 10
key Tab
key Tab
focus
# Notes reached by this Tab, not read from the page before it.
heard Notes
type hello world
key Left
hold ctrl Left
hold ctrl Left
hold ctrl Right
key End
hold shift Left
key BackSpace
key Return
type two
key Up
key Down
# Said by NVDA in Chrome as by the desktop readers, in this order: the field
# named as the second Tab reaches it, then the words as Control+Left
# reads them back. Text typed into Name, with Notes said only after it,
# fails the walk.
expect Notes
expect world
expect hello
expect two
